	(text "Counter reset needs to go \nto $F not $0 to avoid \nskipping the first pixel"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.716 70.104 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "070229df-2455-47da-8c33-5d8f1d0cc9ff")
	)
	(text "BPP = 0\n\nPixelData = 000.Dn\n\nBPP = 1\n\nPixelData = 00.DDn\n\nBPP = 2\n\nPixelData = DDDDn\n\nBPP = 3 *\n\nPixelData = DDDDDDDD\n\n* Not Used"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.478 14.986 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f154ecd5-b40f-4f78-963a-4b72aef917cb")
	)
	(text_box "The process of selecting the relevant bits from the data register is performed by using a group of multiplexers.\n\nFor 1 BPP a single multiplexer is used. For 2 BPP two multiplexers are needed, selecting alternate bits on each count but out of phase.\n\nFor 4 BPP the system needs four multiplexers, selecting the 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 4th bit, or the 5th, 6th, 7th and 8th bit"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.26 139.7 0)
		(size 48.26 24.13)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5ec7c165-765a-4431-8b60-f78fd67c3201")
	)
	(text_box "The BitmapPixelData module is technically 3 modules in one. Each is responsible for defining the palette index from the current bitmap data\n\nTraditionally the bitmap data would be held in a shift register, rotated out with each pixel transition.\n\nDue to the variable bitmap data length the system uses a multiplexing mechanism to switch between bit positions with an effective data length of 1, 2 or 4 bits. This saves on triggering a variable number of clock pulses to shift sufficient data out of the register holding the bitmap data\n\nThe final element in this is pulling the unused bits of the palette index to 0 so that the lowest 2 or 4 indexes are used. This could be substituted with a control register held value that changes which consecutive sequence is utilised. It still limits the effective palette to a fixed selection but does offer some additional control. This would be more effective if the palette is programmable but in that event the need to use anything more than the lowest palette options is largely negated"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 139.7 0)
		(size 50.8 57.15)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d9aa722e-cc12-47e5-86ea-68be5e9b0848")
	)
